# Text files are LF in every clone (TW28). Git for Windows checks out with CRLF by default (core.autocrlf=true), and `roc fmt --check` and
# the string tests of l0 fail on a CRLF file. The shell scripts and the fixtures (tests/scenarios, tests/commands/cases) are compared byte for byte.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.roc text eol=lf
# Binary fixtures: archives, packages and databases are never changed by a line end rule.
*.tar binary
*.gz binary
*.zst binary
*.xz binary
*.zip binary
*.db binary
*.png binary
